+# Tasks
+
+## 1. Repository layer
+
+- [x] 1.1 Add `OrderRepository.applyCoupon(id, discountCents, finalAmountCents, couponCode)` updating the order row, and verify it with a unit test
+- [x] 1.2 Add `CouponRepository.recordRedemption(orderId, code, discountCents, createdAt)` and `CouponRepository.incrementUsedCount(code)` and verify both with unit tests
+- [x] 1.3 Wrap the order update and redemption writes in a single transaction and verify a failed redemption leaves the order unchanged
+
+## 2. Service layer
+
+- [x] 2.1 Implement discount helper (`FIXED` and `PERCENT` with `maxDiscountCents` and amount cap) and verify with unit tests for each branch
+- [x] 2.2 Implement `OrderService.applyCoupon(id, couponCode)` with validation (exists → 400, ACTIVE → 400, validity window → 400, min amount → 400, usage limit → 400, order missing → 404) and verify tests for each rule
+- [x] 2.3 On success persist discount/coupon/redemption and increment usage, then return the reloaded order; verify `usedCount` increments and the order fields match
+
+## 3. HTTP layer
+
+- [x] 3.1 Register `POST /orders/:id/apply-coupon` in `src/routes/orders.ts`, parse the id and `couponCode`, and verify a valid request returns 200 with the updated order
+- [x] 3.2 Verify unknown/expired/disabled coupons return 400 and an unknown order returns 404 through `app.request(...)`
+
+## 4. Verification
+
+- [x] 4.1 Add `tests/apply-coupon.test.ts` covering the acceptance criteria and run `npm test` to confirm all tests pass
+- [x] 4.2 Run `npm run build` and confirm there are no type errors
+
+## Workflow follow-up
+
+- Archive the change after review requirements are satisfied.
